# Flutter UI

Widgets under `ui/` are presentational. Screens compose them. The widget does not decide how a note is saved.

## Rules

- No `flutter_riverpod` import. No `Provider`, no `Consumer`, no `ref`.
- No repository, no use case, no HTTP client.
- Navigation and saves are callbacks the page passes in, or they do not exist on the widget.
- The widget takes the values it draws (`title`, `body`) and nothing it has to fetch.
- A widget used by one screen stays beside that screen, in the presentation folder for the layout you copied. Move it to `ui/` when a second screen needs it.
- Providers are hand-written Riverpod 3. Do not add `riverpod_annotation` or `build_runner` for providers.

A page test pumps the screen inside `ProviderScope`. A tile test pumps the tile inside a `Scaffold` and no `ProviderScope`. If the tile test needs a provider scope, the widget is no longer presentational.
